From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: miogds <miogds@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:29:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ios: the launcher's Play button compiles for visionOS

visionOS has no Liquid Glass button styles (.glassProminent is unavailable in its SDK), the one error in the front end's Swift sources there. The button takes .borderedProminent on visionOS; iOS is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: visionOS is outside upstream's support matrix: the launcher's Swift sources compile for its SDK
Issue: none yet (miogds/NX2Apple, visionOS evaluation branch; to be filed before this goes to LNPANDY/NX2Apple)

---
 dm/ios/Sources/Launcher.swift | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dm/ios/Sources/Launcher.swift b/dm/ios/Sources/Launcher.swift
index 2e58a9a..4f10125 100644
--- a/dm/ios/Sources/Launcher.swift
+++ b/dm/ios/Sources/Launcher.swift
@@ -228,7 +228,11 @@ private struct LauncherView: View {
 
     @ViewBuilder var playButton: some View {
         let button = Button(action: start) { Text("Play").font(.title3.weight(.semibold)).frame(maxWidth: 220) }.controlSize(.large).disabled(checking)
+        #if os(visionOS)   // no Liquid Glass button styles on visionOS
+        button.buttonStyle(.borderedProminent)
+        #else
         if #available(iOS 26.0, *) { button.buttonStyle(.glassProminent) } else { button.buttonStyle(.borderedProminent) }
+        #endif
         if checking {
             VStack(spacing: 6) {
                 HStack(spacing: 6) { ProgressView(); Text("Checking the cloud save…").font(.callout).foregroundStyle(.secondary) }
